# L §2.4 Values, L §5.16 (tally 2.1.7 R9, issue #148): a discrete distribution over a key list names it as
# written, `[ka, kb]`, in LOAD-UNIT's message. 2.1.6's refcore printed `None`. (Twin: L5_16_sample_type_mix.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [ka, kb]
index js = [ja, jb]
input w[k in ks]: num
input u[j in js]: num
input g: dist

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2026-01-01
  w[ka] = 1
  w[kb] = 1
  u[ja] = 1
  u[jb] = 1
  g = discrete(w[k] for k in ks)

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027
  known 2026-01-01
  g = discrete(w[k] for k in [ka, kb])

ask q: share(g == ka) law 2026-06-30 paths 10 seed 1
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT random fact g mixes sample types: discrete over [ka, kb], ks ...
